+    /// Set whether a surface holds GPU resources.
+    ///
+    /// Unrealizing frees the surface's swap chain, per-frame render targets
+    /// and font atlas textures; realizing rebuilds them. Intended for surfaces
+    /// an embedder keeps alive but hidden indefinitely (background tabs,
+    /// stacked panes), where the per-surface GPU cost dominates. Both calls
+    /// are asynchronous and land on the renderer thread.
+    ///
+    /// The shell and terminal state are unaffected: an unrealized surface
+    /// still reads its pty, and the first frame after realizing reflects
+    /// everything that arrived meanwhile.
+    ///
+    /// The embedder must alternate the two. A repeated call in either
+    /// direction is ignored rather than treated as an error.
+    export fn ghostty_surface_set_realized(surface: *Surface, realized: bool) void {
+        surface.realizedCallback(realized);
+    }
